# Files in .devcontainer/ the image is not built from. Docker skips them, and
# build_inputs_hash.py leaves them out of the build stamp, so editing one does
# not rebuild. kit.env is here because its values reach the build as arguments,
# which the stamp covers separately.
#
# EXACT FILENAMES ONLY. A line with `*`, `/`, `!` or `?` makes the hash fall back
# to the whole directory: a pattern it half-understood could shrink what the
# stamp covers, and a missed rebuild is the failure the stamp exists to prevent.
run.sh
kit.env
devcontainer.json
project.bashrc
build_inputs_hash.py
claude_code_latest.py
read_local_token.py
set-project-name.py
